The input fixtures distributed with replayr are original artificial recordings.
Their generators are included under tools/ or in the test suite. They contain
no published TAS recordings, game ROMs, audiovisual material, or emulator
binaries. They are distributed under replayr's package license.

FORMAT REFERENCES AND SOURCE PROVENANCE

The readers implement file layouts described in public specifications and
upstream serialization code. The references below identify those materials.
The expanded readers are original R implementations; upstream source trees
and privately downloaded recordings are not distributed with this package.
The upstream license notices listed here describe the consulted material,
whose terms vary by project and component.

TASVideos format documentation
  https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources
  FMV: https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/Famtasia/FMV
  FCM: https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/FCEU/FCM
  M64: https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/Mupen/M64
  SMV: https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/Snes9x/SMV
  MAR: https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/Mamerr/Mar
  Additional format-specific references appear in the reader source headers.

FCEUX (FM2 and FM3)
  https://fceux.com/web/FM2.html
  https://github.com/TASEmulators/fceux
  src/movie.cpp, src/movie.h, and src/input/zapper.cpp describe text/binary
  records, TAS Editor boundaries, and Zapper fields. GPL-2.0-or-later.

BizHawk (BK2, BKM, TAS, TASPROJ, and GBMV container structure)
  https://github.com/TASEmulators/BizHawk/tree/ab81ea25762af8ece499ba278e3f5cc3848ec742
  The original BizHawk C# code is MIT-licensed. Controller definitions,
  Bk2Controller, Bk2LogEntryGenerator, and legacy InputAdapters establish
  field identities, serialization order, and axis ranges. Emulation cores
  bundled with BizHawk have their own licenses.

Dolphin (GameCube and Wii DTM)
  https://github.com/dolphin-emu/dolphin
  Source/Core/Core/Movie.cpp and Movie.h; WiimoteCommon/DataReport;
  WiimoteEmu/DesiredWiimoteState, Camera, and Extension/{Nunchuk,Classic}.
  GPL-2.0-or-later. The mixed HID layout follows Dolphin 5.0.
  The extended Zelda Edition layout follows Movie.h in:
  https://github.com/dragonbane0/dolphin/tree/a6e66c227c592d09ff09ef9b238d15ff52dd9632
  GPL-2.0-or-later.

