ZSNES (ZMV)
  https://github.com/emillon/zsnes/blob/master/src/zmovie.c
  Enhanced movie headers, compressed state blocks, controller packing,
  repeat records, and chapter tables. GPL-2.0-only, ZSNES Team.

MAME-rerecording (MAR)
  The reader uses the published MAR structure and factual game port mappings.
  Historical MAME-rr serialization was inspected to verify record boundaries;
  its noncommercial source is not reproduced or translated into the R reader.
  The bundled mar-layouts.json cites each port-order reference and corresponding
  current MAME driver. The inspected current drivers use BSD-3-Clause notices:
  https://github.com/mamedev/mame/tree/master/src/mame

FinalBurn Alpha (FBM)
  The FGK adaptive Huffman decoder is independently implemented from the
  mathematical algorithm described by Jeffrey Scott Vitter (1987), section 2:
  https://doi.org/10.1145/31846.42227
  FBM word order and chunk structure were checked against published recordings.
  Bundled fbm-layouts.json contains factual input-field order, names, and types
  with source references. No emulator decompressor implementation is included.

Dustmod (DFT)
  https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/Dustmod
  https://dustkidblog.wordpress.com/2016/08/07/nexus-tasing-with-dustmod/
  Script syntax, archive structure, and input commands. Directional double-tap
  encoding is documented by Dusted's exporter and tests:
  https://github.com/AlexMorson/dusted/blob/af0a8f57a12f5b6986c9791c64bef7578e192acb/src/dusted/nexus_script.py
  Dusted uses the MIT license, Alex Morson. The R reader independently parses
  the script syntax and retains commands as data.


libTAS (LTM)
  https://github.com/clementgallet/libTAS/blob/master/src/program/movie/InputSerialization.cpp
  src/shared/inputs/{AllInputs,SingleInput,ControllerInputs,InputEvent} describe
  field names and controller ranges. GPL-3.0-or-later, Clement Gallet.

Hourglass (WTF and HGM)
  https://tasvideos.org/EmulatorResources/Hourglass/WTF
  Public format specification; TASVideos documentation uses CC-BY 2.0:
  https://tasvideos.org/SiteLicense
  The reader follows the documented header and frame packet layout.

